This is v1 of the dataset for the VBLL model using MINERvA dataset. The format is:
#evt, 2,
#1, muon, Emu true (value from truth_muon_E), pmux true (truth_muon_px), pmuy, pmuz, #2, proton Ep true (value from truth_proton_E), ppx true (truth_proton_px), ppy true, ppz true
#1, muon, Emu (value from MasterAnaDev_muon_E), pmux (MasterAnaDev_muon_Px), pmuy, pmuz, #2, proton, Ep (value from MasterAnaDev_proton_E_fromdEdx), ppx (MasterAnaDev_proton_Px_fromdEdx), ppy, ppz

This is the same format as v0, with ~60x more stat. This is the full stat for NDP.
Please note this will be different from the dataset you'll get in August in:
1. There is no PID likelihood
2. There is no mis-match

evt i, n true particles, l reconstructed particles, vertex x, vertex y, vertex z
1st true, PID 1, PID 2,... PID 6, px, py, pz,
2nd true, PID 1, PID 2,... PID 6, px, py, pz,
...
nth true, PID 1, PID 2,... PID 6, px, py, pz,
1st reco, PID 1, PID 2,... PID 6, px, py, pz,
2nd reco, PID 1, PID 2,... PID 6, px, py, pz,
...
lth reco, PID 1, PID 2,... PID 6, px, py, pz,
#1, muon, Emu true (value from truth_muon_E), pmux true (truth_muon_px), pmuy, pmuz, #2, proton Ep true (value from truth_proton_E), ppx true (truth_proton_px), ppy true, ppz true
#1, muon, Emu (value from MasterAnaDev_muon_E), pmux (MasterAnaDev_muon_Px), pmuy, pmuz, #2, proton, Ep (value from MasterAnaDev_proton_E_fromdEdx), ppx (MasterAnaDev_proton_Px_fromdEdx), ppy, ppz

